ave been a  sign of anything it's that  every time the government ups the  pressure on the protesters they just  bring out more people against them  and we just heard in the report that  security forces are targeting  women why is that  well i think these women's marches  women's demonstrations even if they  haven't been as big as the sunday  demonstrations they really have  played a very important role in social  media they've inspired a lot of people  the women they're very keen to show that  protests can be safe that protests can  be  without violence bringing their children  bringing flowers trying to create a  different atmosphere the government here  has tried to cast protesters violent  attempts to  interfere in belarus affairs something  that people nor ordinary people should  keep away from  and i think their example is really  infectious i was walking with them  yesterday and you saw people  standing on their balconies waving  flowers surprised that the protests had  come  out into the suburbs where they live  that protest is not just something they  see on their  phone screens their tv screens but  something that can happen in real  everyday life  and the most impressive thing for me or  surprising even was that after those  arrests we saw in the report  the women who were left didn't leave  that spot they just stayed so about half  an hour later the police had to come  back and arrest yet more people  i think they seemed themselves shocked  that those pretty violent arrests had  not had a chilling effect on them and  they were just  willing to keep on standing there and  basically stare the police down  all right dw's nick connolly in thanks  for that reporting  you

